    "q-212364": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212364",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Written in **ascending order**, the solutions to $|2-k|=9$ are $k=${{field-1}} and $k=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|2-k|=2-k,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2-k| & =9 \\\\ 2-k & =9 \\\\ -k & =7 \\\\ k & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|2-k|=-(2-k),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2-k| & =9 \\\\ -(2-k) & =9 \\\\ -2+k & =9 \\\\ k & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $k=-7$ and $k=11.$",
