    "q-154692": {
      "dom_id": "step-q154692",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "If $|\\frac{7}{5}z+3|=1,$ then $z=$",
      "worked_solution": "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|\\frac{7}{5}z+3|=\\frac{7}{5}z+3,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{7}{5}z+3| & =1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{5}z+3 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{5}z & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $\\frac{5}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{5}z & =-2 \\\\ (\\frac{5}{7})\\cdot (\\frac{7}{5}z) & =(\\frac{5}{7})\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (\\cancel{\\frac{5}{7}})\\cdot (\\cancel{\\frac{7}{5}}z) & =-\\frac{10}{7} \\\\ z & =-\\frac{10}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|\\frac{7}{5}z+3|=-(\\frac{7}{5}z+3),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{7}{5}z+3| & =1 \\\\ -(\\frac{7}{5}z+3) & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{5}z-3 & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{5}z & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $-\\frac{5}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{5}z & =4 \\\\ (-\\frac{5}{7})\\cdot (-\\frac{7}{5}z) & =(-\\frac{5}{7})\\cdot (4) \\\\ (\\cancel{-\\frac{5}{7}})\\cdot (\\cancel{-\\frac{7}{5}}z) & =-\\frac{20}{7} \\\\ z & =-\\frac{20}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=-\\frac{20}{7}$ and $z=-\\frac{10}{7}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
